{"format":"long","channel":"history","style":"mapminutes","voice":"bm_george","speed":1.05,"projection":"canada","id":"mm-canada-empty","title":"Why Is Canada So Empty? The Map Has the Answer","summary":"Two in three Canadians live within 100 km of the US border, on about 4% of the land. The rest of Canada is frozen ground, bare rock and very little farmland, and that is why the cities line up along the border.","tags":["why is canada so empty","canada population","canada map","canadian shield","permafrost","geography","map minutes"],"intro_chapter":"Two in three, one strip","thumbnail":{"words":["66%","LIVE","HERE"],"expr":"surprised","cam":{"fit":[-126,43.0,-60,63.0],"pad":-0.04},"layers":{"strip":{"opacity":0.9}},"callout":{"at":[-79.4,43.7],"arrow_from":[1012,388],"bend":40},"ax":700,"ay":372,"fw":1260,"pin_x":200,"pin_y":705,"pin_r":160,"words_top":40,"words_right":50,"words_fs":118,"needle":120,"lean":6},"sources":["Two out of three people (66%) lived within 100 km of the southern Canada-US border, an area that represents about 4% of Canada's territory; 3.9 people per square km vs 35.3 in the US; a large land area (close to 9 million square km) (Statistics Canada, The Daily, 8 Feb 2017, 2016 Census): https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/170208/dq170208a-eng.htm","Approximately 0.3% of Canadians or 118,000 people were living in the three territories; nearly three in four Canadians lived in one of Canada's 41 large urban centres; Nunavut 36,858 (Statistics Canada, The Daily, 9 Feb 2022, 2021 Census): https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/220209/dq220209a-eng.htm","About 50 per cent of Canada is underlain by permafrost (40-50 per cent in the Regions section) (The Canadian Encyclopedia, Permafrost, edited 10 Aug 2015): https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/permafrost","At 5 million km2, the Shield makes up roughly 50 per cent of Canada's land mass; bare rock, thin soils, muskeg; thousands of small lakes (The Canadian Encyclopedia, Canadian Shield, edited 11 Aug 2021): https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/shield","In 2021, 6.2% of Canada's land was reported as total farm area (national data exclude the three territories) (Statistics Canada, Canadian Agriculture at a Glance, 20 Oct 2022, 2021 Census of Agriculture): https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/96-325-x/2021001/article/00012-eng.htm","Nunavut land area 2,093,190 km2; population 36,858 (2021 Census) (Canadian Geographic Education, Nunavut infographic, data from Statistics Canada): https://cangeoeducation.ca/en/resources/nunavut-infographic","Map data and city latitudes: Natural Earth (public domain) https://www.naturalearthdata.com and US Census Bureau cartographic boundary files (public domain) https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/carto-boundary-file.html"],"score":[{"scene":0,"mood":"wonder"},{"scene":5,"mood":"explore"},{"scene":12,"mood":"tension"},{"scene":19,"mood":"explore"},{"scene":23,"mood":"payoff"}],"scenes":[{"type":"map","narration":"Two out of three Canadians live in this thin strip.","cam":[{"fit":"canada","pad":0.04,"t":0},{"fit":"canada","pad":-0.01,"t":"end","ease":"sine.inOut"}],"data":{"layers":{"strip":{"lit":true},"border":{"draw":false},"parallel49":{"lit":true}},"labels":[{"text":"2 in 3","at":[-79.4,43.7],"style":"callout","anchor":"n","lit":true}]},"pin":{"expr":"surprised","enter":"drop","acts":[{"t":0.35,"point":[-79.4,43.7],"hold":0}]}},{"type":"map","narration":"The rest of the country, close to {9 million|nine million} square kilometres of land, is mostly empty.","cam":[{"from":"prev","t":0},{"fit":"canada","pad":0.02,"t":"end","ease":"sine.inOut"}],"data":{"layers":{"strip":{"lit":true,"opacity":0.4},"border":{"draw":false},"territories":{"cue":"rest","opacity":0.28}},"labels":[{"text":"~9 million km²","at":[-100.0,62.0],"style":"callout","anchor":"n","cue":"nine"}]},"pin":{"expr":"neutral","acts":[{"t":0.3,"look":[2,-9]},{"cue":"empty","expr":"worried"}]}},{"type":"pin","n